{ dg-modules "rcprelude" }
{ Rosetta Code, task "Even or odd", ALGOL 68 solution even-or-odd.alg.
  https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Even_or_odd#ALGOL_68
  The text of Rosetta Code is available under the GNU Free Documentation
  License 1.3 (see README.md).  The solution is unchanged in orig/even-or-odd.a68;
  this copy was prepared for ga68 and converted to SUPPER stropping by
  tools/rosetta_prep.py. }
access Rc_Prelude (
{ Algol 68 has a standard operator: ODD which returns TRUE if its integer  }
{ operand is odd and FALSE if it is even                                   }
{ E.g.:                                                                    }

int n;
print( ( "Enter an integer: " ) );
read( ( n ) );
print( ( whole( n, 0 ), " is ", if ODD n then "odd" else "even" fi, newline ) )
)
